rust.summary:
P4 (structure and edits) is implemented in the Rust core for all of design §4 and addendum items 6, 10 and 11. Every settle command passes. Nothing is committed or pushed.

Structure (4.1/4.4). There are new workbook-level verbs `Workbook::insert_rows`, `remove_rows`, `insert_columns` and `remove_columns`. `rename_sheet`, `remove_sheet` and `move_sheet` now rewrite every carried reference through one adjuster in the new crate-private `excel/shift.rs` (`Axis`, `Band`, `Shift`, `Rewriter`, `SheetEdits`, `DrawingEdits`, `VmlEdits`, `ChartEdits`, `CacheEdits`). The adjuster rewrites once per shape and host class, and records what it cannot reverse so undo can put it back. It moves:
- formulas and defined names;
- CF, DV and x14 formulas and ranges; hyperlinks, including `@location`;
- autoFilter, sortState and filterColumn colId; protected ranges, ignored errors, cell watches, row and column breaks;
- sparklines, tables, comments, VML anchors, drawing anchors, chart `c:f`, pivot cache `worksheetSource` and pivot location;
- merges, the frozen pane and row/column formats.

Blocking elements are refused by name. The XML rewrites go through a new generic byte-preserving editor, `package::edit_document`, with its `Edits`/`Tag` types. Parts it rewrites are kept as workbook overrides until the save. `check_band` reads each related part once and hands it to `plan`.

Deleted: `Sheet::insert_rows` and `Sheet::remove_rows` (no back-compat), plus `Sheet::set_layout`, `rewrite_formulas`, `stands_from` and the `excel_layout` internals module.

Sheet layout (4.2). New public methods: `Sheet::set_frozen`, `set_column_width`, `set_row_height`, `set_columns_hidden`, `set_rows_hidden`, `merge`, `unmerge`, `edge`, and `current_region`, plus the new `Direction` enum. `set_cell` now keeps the style of the cell it replaces.

Ranges (4.3). New:
- `Workbook::clear` with the `Clear` enum;
- `Workbook::paste` with `Paste` (values, formulas or formats; cut-paste retargets references);
- `paste_text`, `sort` with `SortKey`, and `sheet_state`/`set_sheet_state`;
- `Workbook::fill` with `FillMode` (series or copy), in `fill.rs`;
- `Workbook::find` and `replace` with `FindOptions`, `FindScope` and `Within`, in `find.rs`. `find` is the service's find-next read: scope sheet or workbook, `from` exclusive with wrap, values or formulas, matchCase, entireCell, and `~` wildcard escapes.

Edits and undo (4.5/4.6). New in `edit.rs`:
- `Edit`, one variant per service op: `FillEntry` carries `at` and the replace op spells the searched text `text`, plus `Land`, `Batch`, `Restore` and `RestoreSheet`;
- `Applied` (inverse, touched, structural, sheets, styles, bytes, result), `Restore`, `RestoreSheet`, `Landing`, `MAX_EDITED_CELLS`;
- `Workbook::apply`, `Edit::byte_size`, `Edit::label`, `Edit::from_scalar` (sheets by key, located refusals such as `$.edit.entries[3].ref`);
- the internals dump `internals::excel_edit::state`.

New in `journal.rs`: `Journal` (`record`, `undo`, `redo`, `labels`, `len`, `is_empty`, `clear`), `DEFAULT_JOURNAL_ENTRIES` and `DEFAULT_JOURNAL_BYTES`.

Tests:
- A property test applies every Edit variant, undoes it and compares state exactly, then redoes it and compares again.
- Journal bounds are pinned.
- Refusals are atomic.
- Rich-package tests cover the shifts.

Costs:
- New allocations row `excel_structural_edit_allocates_per_shape_and_nothing_per_formula`: the formulas cost 10 extra allocations at both 1,024 and 16,384 rows.
- New iobase_calls row `a_structural_edit_reads_each_part_it_moves_references_in_once`: 14 reads for the first edit, 1 for the second.
- New bench rows: `format_render`, `workbook_set_entry`, `workbook_set_style`, and `workbook_insert_rows_formulas` (100k cells: a number and three formula shapes per row, plus a cross-sheet sheet).

Exchange: this crate opens the openpyxl fidelity workbook, inserts row 3 and column A on `Data`, and saves it. openpyxl then asserts the formulas on both sheets, CF, DV, hyperlinks, autofilter, table, merge, frozen pane, and row and column sizes all shifted exactly. The Rust half also checks the `_xlnm._FilterDatabase` name, which openpyxl does not read back.
